From af23f7e15be4bf098a706046763bbc848245bed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Skowronski <jakub.skowronski@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:16:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(ec): total capture equals the sum of its final states
 with external capture on

A total-capture segment is an incoherent sum over the capture pairs, so with
external capture on it must still equal the sum of the single-pair segments of
the same model, whatever other segments the project holds.  On 13C(p,g)14N at
E_cm = 46 keV, AZURE2 7e533b7 (the version the website pins) gave a total of
6.59 or 7.225 keV b against a sum of 8.494, depending on which other segments
were present.

Cause, fixed on dev by 886cdf7: CountECAmplitudes left out the component
amplitudes that InitializeComponentSegments appends to intEC.dat/.extrap, so
every reuse of a file was rejected and the data-segment part rewritten.  The
component pass then re-read USE_PREVIOUS_INTEGRALS and read the rewritten file
from its start as if it were the component part.  pyazr asks for reuse
whenever output/intEC.dat exists, so every run after the first in a project
directory was affected.  On dev the total equals the sum (8.4942 with and
without the single-pair segments, fresh and reused).

tests/total_capture_ec locks this in: a 13C+p model with three capture pairs
(gamma0, gamma 2.313, gamma 3.948, ANCs on all three final states), in data
and extrapolation mode, fresh, with a rejected file, and with its own file
reused; the total alone, the total listed first and point mapping off must all
give the same total.  It fails on 7e533b7 (8 of 22 checks, the total off by
3-17 %) and passes on dev.

Also: the component-segment pass in InitializeComponentSegments skipped mapped
points and carried a mapped-point copy loop whose condition
(mappedPoint < GetMappedPoints().begin()) never held.  Component points are
never mapped (MapData skips segments with components and the components are
not in GetSegments()), so neither had any effect, but WalkECAmplitudes counts
every component point.  The pass now computes, writes and reads every point,
as CalculateECAmplitudes does for data segments, and the dead loop is gone.
Output of all eight website evaluations (data and extrapolation, fresh and
reused) is byte-identical to dev.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TkWK4BAGQtHwuzdXYr3xtP
